$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.GOTIP)[8] = "Make sure you have the right spec. Take moves that scale with your class, for example, don\'t take \'Magic Bolt\' if you are a Destroyer. Think about your kill-order as well, and use your defensive abiltiy.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.GOTIP)[12] = "Assassins hit hard and are hard to hit. \'Quick Strike\' and all magic spells have a speed multiplier, so using them will allow you to hit more. Try to outlast his speed buff when he uses it.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.GOTIP)[14] = "The two zombies can do one hell of a stun-lock on you at the start. Just survive their initial burst and their heavy attacks will be on cooldown.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.GOTIP)[18] = "Always counter Sensei\'s \'Enrage\' with either a dispel, or a stun, or else he will one-shot someone. Make sure you have a way to regen your Focus, and don\'t let you or Veradux drop too low on Health.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.GOTIP)[24] = "There is a cheap defensive set for sale. If you have trouble with rock golems, just buy it, it will make a big difference.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.GOTIP)[20] = "There is a cheap defensive set for sale. If you have trouble with rock golems, just buy it, it will make a big difference.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.GOTIP)[23] = "There is a cheap defensive set for sale. If you have trouble with rock golems, just buy it, it will make a big difference.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.GOTIP)[39] = "In case you didn\'t know, Piercing multiplies damage AFTER the static increase. Use high Piercing.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.GOTIP)[40] = "He heals himself at 99%. Timing and planning is important.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH).ENDING = "Congratulations! You have finshed the game. Go to ArmorGames.com for more awesome games, and to check for updates on Sonny! If you still want to play there is one last challenge, but I\'m warning you it is hard! If you continue you play, you will enter Zone 4, where you will have your entire team of six characters to gear up and choose from. You will face four tough bosses, and a training mode that scales endlessly with your level. THIS IS NOT PART OF THE STORY! It is just there for fun! Good luck, and thanks for playing! See you again next time!";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH).MANUAL = new Array();
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH).MANUALEX = new Array();
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.MANUAL)[0] = "How do I play?";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.MANUALEX)[0] = "You can just start a new game right now! All the basics will be explained within the first few fights. Just listen to the dialogue and read the text. Sonny is a turn based fighting game. You choose what move your character makes in his turn by first selecting WHO you want to make a move on, and then you can choose WHAT you want to do to that target. For example, if you want to attack an enemy, you click on the enemy first, then you can choose to attack him. If you want to heal a team mate, select that character and you will be able to choose a move to use on him. You may only have 8 moves \'equipped\' in any fight, and you configure this from your Abilities menu. Some moves can be equipped more than once, so that you can use it more often.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.MANUAL)[1] = "What do the colors on the buffs and numbers mean?";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.MANUALEX)[1] = "They just indicate the element that the ability is classified as: Physical, Magic, Fire, Ice, Lightning, Earth, Shadow, and Poison.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.MANUAL)[2] = "Piercing and Defense?";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.MANUALEX)[2] = "Piercing determines how much damage an element does, the chances of that element scoring a critical hit, and how much damage a critical hit adds. This is indicated visually on the bar graph, from 0% to 100%. Defense operates in a similar way, but as a counter to Piercing.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.MANUAL)[3] = "What does each stat do?";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.MANUALEX)[3] = "Strength and Magic are just co-efficients for your abilities. Speed is also a co-efficient, but to only a few abilities. Speed also increases your Piercing (1 point for every 2 points of Speed) and dodge/accuracy. Vitality increases your Health by 8 points.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.MANUAL)[4] = "Help! I am stuck on a level!";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH?.MANUALEX)[4] = "It\'s mainly about the Strategy and spec that you use. Observe the enemy carefully, and look into your entire Ability tree to find ways to beat them.";
$$o(KrinLang?.ENGLISH).EXPLAINEXTRA = "Please select a topic.";
$$o(KrinLang).GERMAN = new Object();
